  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "A one-run lead through six innings became three runs in the seventh, and then it all evaporated in the tenth.",
    "what_this_means": "This team had the moments. Lee's homer, Gilbert's go-ahead swing. But couldn't finish the game. They converted one runner home across six RISP situations while Houston's bullpen let the game slip away after the lead changed. By the time the ninth inning ended tied, the tenth belonged entirely to Houston. Three runs scored before the Giants recorded an out, and by then the game was already gone. Drew Gilbert drove in two runs and briefly had them ahead, but one man's production against a parade of runners left stranded is not a formula that holds. They had their window in the seventh and eighth. The lineup didn't stay in it long enough.",
    "what_to_watch": "Hunter Brown takes the mound tonight for Houston with a 3.53 ERA. The Giants need to solve early innings. They've been chasing since the first inning too many times this week.",
